IX["EHSAN-ANAT-PHARYNX-MCQ-"] = {
  1: ["**Stylopharyngeus** is supplied by the **glossopharyngeal** nerve, not the pharyngeal plexus.", "a: Superior constrictor: pharyngeal plexus (vagus).", "b: Inferior constrictor: pharyngeal plexus (plus external/recurrent laryngeal).", "d: Palatopharyngeus: pharyngeal plexus."],
  3: ["The **superior constrictor** arises from the pterygoid hamulus, **pterygomandibular raphe** and mandible (the raphe also gives origin to buccinator).", "a: Stylopharyngeus arises from the styloid process.", "b: The middle constrictor arises from the hyoid and stylohyoid ligament.", "c: Palatopharyngeus arises from the palate."],
  5: ["The **internal laryngeal nerve and superior laryngeal vessels** pass through the gap between the **middle and inferior** constrictors (piercing the thyrohyoid membrane).", "b: The inferior laryngeal artery passes **below** the inferior constrictor with the recurrent laryngeal nerve.", "c: The ascending palatine artery passes **above** the superior constrictor.", "d: The auditory tube passes **above** the superior constrictor."],
  7: ["The **palatoglossal** arch (anterior pillar) and **palatopharyngeal** arch (posterior pillar) bound the tonsillar fossa.", "a: Styloglossus and stylopharyngeus are not pillars.", "c: Salpingopharyngeus runs from the auditory tube, not a pillar.", "d: The constrictors form the tonsil's **bed**, not its pillars."],
  9: ["The **palatoglossal fold** (arch) is the anterior boundary of the tonsillar fossa.", "b: The palatopharyngeal fold is the **posterior** boundary.", "c: The soft palate is above.", "d: The dorsum of the tongue is below."],
  10: ["The **oropharynx** gets its sensory supply from the **glossopharyngeal** nerve (the gag reflex afferent).", "a: Stylopharyngeus is supplied by the **glossopharyngeal**.", "b: The constrictors are supplied by the **vagus** (cranial accessory fibres via the pharyngeal plexus), not the spinal accessory.", "c: Palatopharyngeus is supplied by the vagus."],
  11: ["The pharyngeal wall is **deficient in front**, where it opens into the nasal cavity, mouth and larynx.", "a: It becomes the oesophagus opposite **C6** (lower border of the cricoid).", "c: The constrictors are supplied by the **vagus** (pharyngeal plexus).", "d: The oropharyngeal isthmus is bounded by the **palatoglossal** arches."],
  12: ["The palatine tonsil drains to the **jugulodigastric** (tonsillar) node — the node that swells in tonsillitis.", "a: It lies medial to the **superior** constrictor.", "b: It lies between the **palatoglossus and palatopharyngeus** arches.", "c: Its main supply is the **tonsillar branch of the facial** artery."],
  13: ["The 3rd gap (between middle and inferior constrictors) transmits the **superior laryngeal artery** with the internal laryngeal nerve.", "a: The ascending pharyngeal artery runs up outside the pharynx.", "b: The ascending palatine passes through the **1st** gap (above the superior constrictor).", "d: The inferior laryngeal artery passes through the **4th** gap (below the inferior constrictor)."],
};

IX["EHSAN-ANAT-NOSE-MCQ-"] = {
  2: ["The **posterior ethmoidal** air cells open into the **superior meatus**.", "a: The frontal sinus opens into the **middle** meatus (frontonasal duct/infundibulum).", "b: The maxillary sinus opens into the **middle** meatus (hiatus semilunaris).", "c: Anterior and middle ethmoidal cells open into the **middle** meatus."],
  3: ["The **sphenoidal** sinus opens into the **sphenoethmoidal recess**, above the superior concha.", "a: Frontal → middle meatus.", "b: Maxillary → middle meatus.", "c: Anterior/middle ethmoidal → middle meatus."],
  4: ["The maxillary ostium opens into the **hiatus semilunaris** of the **middle meatus** — a mass there blocks it.", "a: The inferior meatus receives the nasolacrimal duct.", "c: The superior meatus receives the posterior ethmoidal cells.", "d: The nasopharynx is behind the nasal cavity."],
  5: ["**Little's area** (Kiesselbach's plexus) is on the **antero-inferior nasal septum**, where several arteries anastomose.", "a: The roof is the cribriform plate.", "b: The floor is the palate.", "d: The lateral wall carries the conchae."],
  7: ["The **middle ethmoidal** cells open on (or above) the **bulla ethmoidalis**.", "a: The maxillary opens into the hiatus semilunaris.", "b: The frontal opens into the front of the middle meatus.", "c: The anterior ethmoidal cells open into the hiatus/infundibulum."],
  8: ["Pain in the upper teeth with a tender maxilla but healthy teeth = **maxillary sinusitis** (the superior alveolar nerves run in its walls; the tooth roots bulge into its floor).", "a: Sphenoid sinusitis gives deep/vertex headache.", "b: Ethmoidal sinusitis gives pain between the eyes.", "d: Frontal sinusitis gives forehead pain and tenderness."],
  9: ["The **nasolacrimal duct** opens into the **inferior meatus**.", "a: The septum is often **deviated**; it is rarely exactly midline.", "b: Epistaxis is commonest at the **antero-inferior** septum (Little's area).", "d: Lymph from the vestibule drains to the **submandibular** nodes."],
  10: ["The **sphenoid** sinus opens into the sphenoethmoidal recess.", "a: Frontal → middle meatus.", "b: Maxillary → middle meatus.", "c: Anterior ethmoidal → middle meatus."],
  12: ["The roof of the maxillary sinus is the floor of the orbit, carrying the **infraorbital** nerve in its groove/canal.", "a: The anterior superior alveolar runs in the **anterior** wall.", "b: The middle superior alveolar runs in the **lateral/anterior** wall.", "c: The posterior superior alveolar runs in the **posterior** wall."],
  13: ["Below the vocal folds the laryngeal mucosa is supplied by the **recurrent laryngeal** nerve.", "b: The superior laryngeal is the parent of the internal (sensory, above the folds) and external branches.", "c: The external laryngeal is motor to cricothyroid.", "d: The internal laryngeal supplies **above** the folds.", "e: The pharyngeal nerve does not supply the larynx."],
  14: ["The **lateral cricoarytenoid** rotates the arytenoids medially: **adduction**.", "a: Thyroarytenoid mainly **relaxes/shortens** the folds.", "c: Posterior cricoarytenoid is the only **abductor**.", "d: Vocalis fine-tunes tension."],
  15: ["The **posterior cricoarytenoids** are the only muscles that **open** (abduct) the vocal folds.", "b: Lateral cricoarytenoids **close** them.", "c: Thyroarytenoids **relax** them.", "d: The transverse arytenoid **closes** the back of the glottis."],
  16: ["Recurrent laryngeal injury paralyses the **posterior cricoarytenoid** — the only **abductor** of the cords.", "b: Lateral cricoarytenoid is an adductor.", "c: Thyroarytenoid is a relaxer.", "d: Cricothyroid (external laryngeal) is a tensor and is spared in recurrent injury."],
  17: ["**Posterior cricoarytenoid** abducts the vocal folds.", "a: Cricothyroid **tenses** them.", "c: Lateral cricoarytenoid **adducts** them.", "d: Aryepiglottic closes the laryngeal inlet."],
  18: ["Below the vocal folds: **recurrent laryngeal** nerve.", "b: The superior laryngeal's internal branch supplies above the folds.", "c: The external laryngeal is motor.", "d: The internal laryngeal supplies above the folds."],
  19: ["**Bilateral partial** recurrent laryngeal injury paralyses the abductors first (Semon's law) → both cords lie near the midline → **stridor**.", "a: Above the cords is the **internal** laryngeal nerve.", "c: All intrinsic muscles are supplied by the **recurrent** laryngeal nerve except cricothyroid.", "d: Cricothyroid is supplied by the **external** laryngeal nerve."],
  20: ["The cricoid cartilage lies at **C6** (where the larynx becomes the trachea and the pharynx the oesophagus).", "a: C2 is the axis.", "b: C4 is the level of the thyroid cartilage's upper border.", "d: T2 is at the level of the suprasternal notch, in the thorax — too low."],
  21: ["The **tympanic membrane** forms most of the **lateral** wall of the middle ear.", "a: The medial wall has the promontory and windows.", "c: The floor (jugular wall) overlies the internal jugular vein.", "d: The anterior (carotid) wall has the auditory tube opening."],
  22: ["The roof of the middle ear is the **tegmen tympani** (thin bone separating it from the middle cranial fossa).", "a: The lateral wall is the **tympanic membrane**.", "c: The medial wall is the labyrinthine wall (promontory, oval and round windows); the ossicles lie in the cavity.", "d: The promontory is on the **medial** wall."],
  23: ["Hearing loss + taste loss + facial weakness = a lesion at the **internal acoustic meatus** (VII and VIII).", "a: Foramen ovale: V3.", "b: Foramen spinosum: middle meningeal artery.", "d: Foramen rotundum: V2."],
  25: ["The **anterior tympanic** artery (maxillary artery, 1st part) supplies the middle ear through the petrotympanic fissure.", "~d: Also accepted: the **posterior auricular** artery's stylomastoid branch also supplies the middle ear and mastoid.", "a: The ascending palatine supplies the palate and tonsil.", "b: The tonsillar artery supplies the tonsil."],
  29: ["The atlanto-occipital joints are **ellipsoid** synovial joints (nodding: flexion–extension).", "b: Pivot is the **median atlanto-axial** joint.", "c: Plane joints are the lateral atlanto-axial joints.", "d: In this course 'condylar' means joints like the TMJ and knee; the atlanto-occipital joint is classed as ellipsoid (some books call ellipsoid joints 'condyloid')."],
  30: ["The **median atlanto-axial** joint (dens in the ring of atlas and transverse ligament) is a **pivot** joint: rotation (saying 'no').", "a: Ellipsoid is the atlanto-occipital.", "c: Plane is the lateral atlanto-axial.", "d: Condylar is not this joint."],
  31: ["The **superficial cervical** nodes lie along the **external jugular** vein on the sternomastoid.", "a: Nodes along the subclavian vein are supraclavicular/apical.", "b: The **deep** cervical nodes lie along the internal jugular. On the Nov 2024 paper the stem was corrected to “deep” during the exam, which made this the answer there: read the adjective.", "d: Anterior cervical nodes lie along the anterior jugular vein."],
  33: ["The **submental** nodes drain the **tip of the tongue**, the chin, the central lower lip and floor of the mouth.", "b: The forehead drains to parotid (preauricular) nodes.", "c: The parotid drains to parotid and deep cervical nodes.", "d: The lateral nasal wall drains to submandibular/retropharyngeal nodes.", "e: The nasal cavity drains to retropharyngeal and deep cervical nodes.", "f: **Upper** incisors drain to the submandibular nodes (lower incisors go to submental)."],
  36: ["The nerve of the **2nd** pharyngeal arch is the **facial** nerve.", "a: Vagus: 4th and 6th arches.", "b: Mandibular: 1st arch.", "c: Glossopharyngeal: 3rd arch."],
  37: ["A branchial fistula from the neck (front of sternomastoid) to the tonsillar fossa = persistent **cervical sinus** opening into the **2nd pharyngeal pouch** (tonsillar fossa).", "a: The arch itself does not form the tract.", "b: The groove is the outer end; the tract is the cervical sinus.", "c: The 3rd pouch forms the thymus and inferior parathyroids."],
  38: ["Cleft lip = failure of the **maxillary prominence** to fuse with the **intermaxillary segment** (merged medial nasal prominences).", "b: The two medial nasal prominences fuse **with each other** to make the intermaxillary segment.", "c: Lateral and medial nasal failure gives a nasal/oblique facial cleft, not the usual lip cleft.", "d: 'Lateral prominences' alone do not form the upper lip."],
  39: ["The middle-ear cavity (and auditory tube) comes from the **1st pouch** (tubotympanic recess).", "b: 2nd pouch: palatine tonsil.", "c: 3rd pouch: thymus and inferior parathyroid.", "d: 4th pouch: superior parathyroid (and ultimobranchial body)."],
  40: ["1st-arch muscles: **muscles of mastication**, **anterior belly of digastric**, mylohyoid, tensor tympani, tensor palati.", "a: Incomplete — the anterior digastric is also 1st arch.", "c: The **posterior** belly is 2nd arch.", "d: Geniohyoid is from occipital somites (C1)."],
  41: ["The lower lip (and chin, lower jaw) develops from the **mandibular** prominences.", "a: Maxillary prominences form the sides of the upper lip.", "b: The frontonasal prominence forms the forehead and nose.", "c: Medial nasal prominences form the philtrum."],
  43: ["**Stylohyoid** is a 2nd-arch muscle (with facial muscles, posterior digastric, stapedius).", "a: The incus is 1st arch.", "b: The anterior digastric is 1st arch.", "c: Meckel's cartilage is the 1st-arch cartilage."],
  44: ["The **2nd pouch** forms the palatine tonsil (tonsillar fossa).", "a: 1st: tubotympanic recess.", "c: 3rd: thymus + inferior parathyroid.", "d: 4th: superior parathyroid."],
  46: ["The thymus comes from the **3rd pouch** (ventral part); its absence (with parathyroid loss) is DiGeorge syndrome.", "a: 1st: middle ear.", "b: 2nd: palatine tonsil.", "d: 4th: superior parathyroid."],
  47: ["1st-arch muscles are the **muscles of mastication** (+ anterior digastric, mylohyoid, tensors).", "b: Facial muscles are 2nd arch.", "c: Cricothyroid is 4th arch.", "d: The posterior digastric is 2nd arch."],
  48: ["The nerve of the **3rd** arch is the **glossopharyngeal**.", "a: Mandibular: 1st arch.", "b: Facial: 2nd arch.", "d: Vagus: 4th and 6th arches."],
  51: ["**Meckel's cartilage** is the cartilage of the **1st** arch (it gives the malleus and incus).", "a: The stapes is 2nd arch.", "c: Facial muscles are 2nd arch.", "d: The posterior digastric is 2nd arch."],
  52: ["The **masseter** is a muscle of mastication → **1st** arch.", "a: Orbicularis oris is a facial muscle → 2nd arch.", "b: The posterior digastric → 2nd arch.", "c: The stapes → 2nd arch."],
  53: ["**Occipitofrontalis** is a muscle of facial expression → **2nd** arch (facial nerve).", "a: Trapezius comes from occipital somites/lateral plate (accessory nerve).", "b: Temporalis is 1st arch.", "d: Tongue muscles come from occipital myotomes (hypoglossal)."],
  54: ["2nd arch nerve = **facial**.", "a: Mandibular = 1st.", "b: Glossopharyngeal = 3rd.", "d: The oculomotor is not an arch nerve."],
  55: ["3rd arch nerve = **glossopharyngeal**.", "a: Vagus = 4th/6th.", "c: Mandibular = 1st.", "d: The maxillary nerve belongs to the 1st arch too (maxillary process)."],
  56: ["The **2nd pouch** gives the primordium of the **palatine tonsil**.", "b: Pouches are lined with **endoderm** (clefts with ectoderm).", "c: The 4th pouch gives the **superior** parathyroid; the 3rd gives the inferior.", "d: The 1st **pouch** gives the tubotympanic recess; the 1st cleft gives the external acoustic meatus."],
  57: ["The **thymus** arises from the **ventral** part of the **3rd** pouch.", "a: The tubotympanic recess is from the **1st** pouch.", "b: The palatine tonsil is from the **2nd** pouch.", "d: The dorsal 3rd pouch gives the **inferior** parathyroid; the superior comes from the 4th."],
};
